        </div>
        <h3>The expense ledger</h3>
        <p>Your own categories: salaries, rent, utilities, repairs, whatever your school spends on. A category can be retired but never deleted, because deleting one would orphan every old entry filed under it and change last year's figures.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card__icon" style="background: var(--money-50); color: var(--money-700);">
          <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 8h14M5 8a2 2 0 110-4h14a2 2 0 110 4M5 8v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V8m-9 4h4"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Cash drawer sessions</h3>
        <p>A collector opens a drawer, takes fees, and closes it by counting what is there. A difference between the counted cash and the receipts is not rounded away: it is recorded with a written reason, which is the whole point of counting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card__icon card__icon--accent">
          <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8 7V3m8 4V3m-9 8h10M5 21h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>The day book</h3>
        <p>Everything that moved today, in one list, with who entered it. It is the screen a principal opens at six o'clock, and the one that makes a question about a particular receipt answerable in seconds.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card__icon">
          <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 4.354a4 4 0 110 5.292M15 21H3v-1a6 6 0 0112 0v1zm0 0h6v-1a6 6 0 00-9-5.197M13 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0z"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Staff and payroll</h3>
        <p>Staff records, salaries, staff attendance with a daily check in code, and printable staff cards. Teacher logins are tied to the classes each teacher actually teaches, and a leaving date closes the login.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Two honest limits</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px;max-width:64ch">
      Because finding out on a Monday morning is worse than reading it here.
    </p>
    <ul class="checklist" style="margin-top:22px">
      <li>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <span><b>This is not a general ledger.</b> There is no double entry, no trial balance and no chart of accounts. It answers what came in, what went out and what is left, which is the question a school office actually has.</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <span><b>The statement is not a bank document.</b> A printed account statement says so at the bottom, because a parent will one day take it to a bank and be turned away, and it is better that the paper says why.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

